Title = {Exporting Athena Swan? The Politics of Supporting Academic Mothers},
Journal = {POLITICS \& GENDER},
Year = {2026},
Month = {2026 JUN 9},
Abstract = {In a profession designed for men with housewives, academic mothers
   continue to shoulder a disproportionate burden. Motherhood penalties in
   academia are well-documented, with research consistently showing
   negative impacts on mothers' publication rates (Di Leo et al. n.d.;
   Lutter and Schr \& ouml;der 2020; Morgan et al. 2021), citations (Lawson
   et al. 2021), and promotion trajectories (Antecol et al. 2018; Finkel
   and Olswang 1996; Mason et al. 2019) - effects not observed among
   fathers. In recent years, both institutional frameworks and grassroots
   movements have sought to address these inequities, yet their strategies
   and impacts differ significantly.},
