Title = {The White House Gender Policy Council},
Journal = {POLITICS \& GENDER},
Year = {2026},
Month = {2026 APR 16},
Abstract = {The White House Gender Policy Council (GPC) was established by President
   Joe Biden in 2021. It built on earlier offices like the White House
   Council on Women and Girls, which was created during the Barack Obama
   administration but was dissolved under the first Donald Trump
   administration, and the White House Office for Women's Initiatives and
   Outreach, which existed during the Bill Clinton administration but was
   eliminated by the George W. Bush administration. The GPC was responsible
   for the advancement of gender equity and equality in both domestic and
   foreign policy. Jennifer Klein (JK) and Rachel Vogelstein (RV) served,
   respectively, as Director and Deputy Director until the GPC was
   dismantled by the second Trump administration in 2025. This is a
