   on hearing that the \#MeToo movement had extended even into China. The
   ideas in this Critical Perspectives collection go much deeper into the
   nature of and reasons for descriptive representation than I could two
   decades ago. Anne Phillips (1995) and Melissa Williams (1998), the two
   pioneers in this field who produced analyses far more thorough than
   mine, would, I think, agree with me on this. So would Iris Marion Young,
   whose early challenge in a talk over lunch inspired me to puzzle out my
   own take on the problem.},
